{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Wine or strong drink.</b> Wine — by way of its intoxicating effect (Sifra)." "<b>When you come into the Tent of Meeting.</b> I have only 'when you come into the sanctuary' — from where do I derive approaching the altar? 'Entry of the Tent of Meeting' is stated here, and 'entry of the Tent of Meeting' is stated in the consecration of hands and feet — just as there, approaching the altar is treated as entry of the Tent of Meeting, so here too, approaching the altar is treated as entry of the Tent of Meeting (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:38.028010517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}